tory/_/id/50506952/sources-butch-jones-arkansas-state-coach","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5173431/wayshawn-parker","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wayshawn_Parker"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Wayshawn Parker","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wayshawn_Parker","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:36Z","intro":"Wayshawn Parker is an American college football running back for the Utah Utes. He previously played for the Washington State Cougars.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Hailing from Sacramento, California, Parker initially attended Rosemont High School, where he played fullback and linebacker for two seasons."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"WASHINGTON STATE\nIn week two of the 2024 season, Parker rushed 11 times for 69 yards and a touchdown in a win over Texas Tech. During the 2024 season, he rushed for 735 yards and four touchdowns on 137 carries, while also hauling in eleven receptions for 108 yards and a touchdown. After the conclusion of the 2024 season, Parker entered his name into the NCAA transfer portal.\n\nUTAH\nOn December 20, 2024, Parker announced that he would transfer to Utah."}]}}